{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.MotivicSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.MotivicSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.nonarchimedean_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.nonarchimedean_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L130-L130","doc":"**Substrate axiom (non-archimedean non-degeneracy).**\n\nAt least one finite place `p` has a non-trivial realization\ntarget.  Together with `archimedean_nontrivial`, this is the\nminimal restricted-product condition of `def:adelic-substrate`:\nthe substrate is genuinely adelic, supported neither entirely\nat `∞` nor entirely on the archimedean continuum, but spread\nacross the archimedean place AND at least one non-archimedean\nplace.\n\nThe full place-compatibility statement — that for every\nmotivic class `x ∈ Mhat` the family `(realize v x)_v` is a\nfinite-support adelic class with almost all finite-place\ncomponents in a designated integral subring — requires the\nauxiliary integral-subring data `Integral : ∀ v, Subring\n(Target v)` and is supplied as a `sorry`-axiom in concrete\ninstances of an extension class (AGENTS.md §3b).\n\nRef: [tate1967]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.archimedean_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.archimedean_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L110-L110","doc":"**Substrate axiom (archimedean non-degeneracy).**\n\nThe archimedean realization target is nontrivial — i.e. the\nsubstrate has a non-degenerate archimedean shadow.  This is\nthe minimal non-vacuous fragment of the Tate factorisation\n`ρ_tot([X]) = (ρ_v([X]))_v` of `def:adelic-substrate`: the\nrestricted product over places assembles a non-trivial\nclassical-limit object only when the archimedean place\ncontributes non-degenerately.\n\nNote: this is genuinely an axiom, not a consequence of\n`lefschetz_invertible`. A trivial `Target Place.infty` (where\n`0 = 1` in the target ring) admits a perfectly valid `RingHom`\nfrom `Mhat` regardless of whether `inclusion lefschetz` is a\nunit in `Mhat`; the existence of `realize Place.infty` does\nnot force `Target Place.infty` to be nontrivial.\n\nRef: [tate1967]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.realize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.realize","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The realization functor at place `v`, taking values in the\ntarget ring `Target v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz_invertible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz_invertible","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L88-L88","doc":"`𝕃` is invertible in `𝓜̂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.inclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.inclusion","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Canonical inclusion `K₀ → 𝓜̂` of the Grothendieck ring into\nthe dimension-completed localization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.lefschetz","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The Lefschetz motive `𝕃 = [𝔸¹] ∈ K₀(Var_k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L47-L131","doc":"**The motivic substrate** (axiomatic class).\n\n`MotivicSubstrate K0 Mhat Target` axiomatises the QOU motivic\nsubstrate over:\n* `K0` — the Grothendieck ring `K₀(Var_k)`.\n* `Mhat` — the dimension-completed localization\n  `𝓜̂ = K₀[𝕃⁻¹]^∧`.\n* `Target : Place → Type*` — the realization target at each\n  place (e.g. `ℝ` at `∞`, `ℚ_p` at finite primes).\n\nFields:\n* `lefschetz : K0` — the Lefschetz motive `𝕃 = [𝔸¹]`.\n* `inclusion : K0 →+* Mhat` — the canonical map into the\n  dimension completion.\n* `lefschetz_invertible` — `𝕃` is a unit in `Mhat`.\n* `realize : (v : Place) → Mhat →+* Target v` — the\n  realization functor at each place.\n\nSubstrate axioms (paired place compatibility): the realization\ntarget is nontrivial at the archimedean place AND at some\nfinite place — the minimal non-vacuous fragment of the Tate\nfactorisation `ρ_tot([X]) = (ρ_v([X]))_v` of\n`def:adelic-substrate`.  This guarantees the substrate is\ngenuinely adelic (supported neither entirely at `∞` nor entirely\nat one finite place) without committing to a specific integral\nsubring data.  The full place-compatibility statement (almost-\nintegral finite-place components for every motivic class)\nrequires auxiliary `Integral : ∀ v, Subring (Target v)` data\nand is supplied as a `sorry`-axiom in concrete instances of\nan extension class.\n\nRef: [kontsevich1995], [denef-loeser2001], [tate1967]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:motivic-substrate","label":"def:motivic-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace.decEq","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instDecidableEqPlace","kind":"instance","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.finite","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.infty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place.infty","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Place","kind":"inductive","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-substrate.lean#L38-L45","doc":"A **place** of `ℚ`: either the archimedean place `∞` or a\nfinite prime `p`. The `finite` constructor takes a\n`Nat.Primes` value (Mathlib subtype `{p : ℕ // p.Prime}`) so\nthat non-prime indices are ruled out at the type level. ","signatureChunk":0}]}